
(8..8) The goal of all pro-independence parties is to celebrate a binding referendum on independence. How to get there, though, is a complex topic. Can the Spanish government really be convinced to hold one? Or is it a non-agreement referendum the only way forward?
(9..9) 1.5 Million march in Barcelona for independence. Will this be our time?
(10..10) "We must *'spanish-ize'* Catalan children." Spanish Minister of Education José Ignacio Wert says. 
(11..11) The "General European Strike" sees thousands in the streets and tens of injured in clashes with police. Esther Quintana, attending the protest, loses an eye due to a rubber bullet fired by the Mossos d'Esquadra.
